WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:07.339
Europium is an element which, when you excite
the atoms or excite the

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:11.210
electrons in the atoms, gives out very nice
red coloured light.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:16.570
Ok, so europium is pretty much in the middle
of the lanthanide series.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:21.140
Perhaps its most famous use is in television
screens.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:26.750
In fact, most or many of the rare earths can
fluoresce in this way and

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:33.330
give out light, but europium is particularly
good at giving a very nice red

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:40.950
colour, and so europium salts are used in
television screens, not LCD

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:46.890
screens like you have on the laptop, but the
old-fashioned cathode ray

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:47.890
televisions.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:51.810
So it’s very good at phosphorescence, for
example, so we use it in the

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:55.070
tubes in TV screens to get different colours.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:00.390
The screen on the inside of the screen you
have dots of europium and

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.429
when the electrons from the electron beam
in the cathode ray tube hit

00:01:04.429 --> 00:01:09.000
the europium you get a very intense emission
of red light which gives

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.470
you the red colour to form the colour television
pictures.

